preConditionHook:
// StopBeyondRangeExtremeAtrBuffer -- Grimes A list (G06-17 / G06-25 / G08-03,
// key StopBeyondRangeExtremeAtrBuffer; also G06-49, key
// StopAfterConsecutiveClosesBeyondLevel, as confirmBars). Authored 2026-09-22 as
// new inputs on StopBeyondRecentRangeExtreme and split out 2026-11-07, because
// the 202611 BRK and OWN templates place StopBeyondRecentRangeExtreme, so that
// rule stays exactly as those families run it. Code otherwise unchanged.
//
// DEFAULTS: bufferAtrMultiple(0.25) is the miner's number (Grimes names no
// multiple), and stopBuffer(0) makes the default the PURE ATR form, as the merged
// pseudocode has it; confirmBars(1) judges the current close alone;
// rangeLookback(20) and atrLookback(14) are unchanged. At bufferAtrMultiple 0
// and confirmBars 1 this is StopBeyondRecentRangeExtreme's behaviour exactly.
//
// Lowest(low[ii+1], rangeLookback) / Highest(high[ii+1], rangeLookback): the
// window ENDS ONE BAR BEFORE THE BAR BEING JUDGED, so no bar can define the
// level it is being tested against. At confirmBars 1 only ii = 0 runs and the
// window is bars 1..rangeLookback, exactly StopBeyondRecentRangeExtreme's.
// Mirrors EasyLanguage's Extremes(): seeded on the first bar of the window,
// scanning the rest, strict comparison so a tie keeps the earliest bar.
// Extremes is EL SOURCE, so its comparisons carry the relational tolerance and
// these use el_lt/el_gt rather than < and >.
//
// TWO GRIMES READINGS, one rule.
//
// (1) bufferAtrMultiple and atrLookback (G06-17 / G06-25 / G08-03, key
// StopBeyondRangeExtremeAtrBuffer). Grimes wants the buffer past the obvious
// level SCALED BY VOLATILITY, not fixed: "a few ticks beyond the obvious
// levels" still gets swept in extra volatility. THE TWO BUFFERS ARE ADDITIVE.
// The merge notes call them alternatives rather than a sum, so the default runs
// the pure ATR form with stopBuffer 0; bufferAtrMultiple 0 turns the ATR buffer
// off and leaves StopBeyondRecentRangeExtreme's fixed price-point buffer. 0.25
// ATR is the miner's number -- Grimes names no multiple. G06-17's extra random
// jitter is NOT carried: strategies must be deterministic.
//
// (2) confirmBars (G06-49, key StopAfterConsecutiveClosesBeyondLevel). "Once
// the market consolidated below that support level the probabilities favoured
// a breakdown, so there was no sense riding the trade to the initial stop."
// A CONSOLIDATION beyond the level, not a poke through it: confirmBars
// consecutive closes each beyond ITS OWN bar's level. confirmBars 1, the
// default, is the single-close test StopBeyondRecentRangeExtreme makes. Grimes
// gives no count; 3 is the miner's.
// EACH BAR IS JUDGED AGAINST THE WINDOW ENDING ONE BAR BEFORE IT, not against
// one frozen level and not against the CURRENT bar's level. The current-level
// reading is unusable: low[1] is inside this bar's window, so
// close[1] <= level - stopBuffer would require close[1] <= low[1] - stopBuffer,
// which no bar can satisfy with a positive buffer -- confirmBars 2 would never
// fire. The at-fill capture the merged pseudocode suggests would make this a
// different machine (an at-entry freeze, which is InitialStopBeyondSwingAtEntry's
// convention), so the rule's own rolling level is kept and simply re-read per
// bar. confirmBars 0 leaves okLong true and fires every bar, so the grid starts
// at 1.
//
// The negated form is exact, not approximate: el_gt is the precise complement
// of el_le under the relational tolerance (el_gt(a,b) is a - b > tol and
// el_le(a,b) is b - a >= -tol), so at confirmBars 1 and bufferAtrMultiple 0
// the long test returns exactly what StopBeyondRecentRangeExtreme's
// el_le(close[0], lowestLow - stopBuffer) does (subtracting 0.0 * atrVal is
// exact).
//
// WFSafe_AvgTrueRange is MultiWalk's ROLLING accumulator, not the built-in it
// resembles: seeded with a full N-term sum on the first calculated bar and
// again whenever the length changes, thereafter updated as TWO statements --
// EL evaluates S[1] + in - out left to right and folding it to S += in - out
// rounds differently. Ported from AtrProfitTarget / SwingPivotTarget. Read once
// per bar into a local, never inside a condition: EL does not short-circuit
// and/or, so an accumulator in a condition would advance on every bar in EL and
// only on some bars here. The local counter is atrLen, not atrLookback:
// atrLookback is this rule's INPUT.
//
// Every scratch value is a localVariables entry, never a hook-scope
// declaration, so the hooks survive a double placement.
//
// Deepest bar touched: max(confirmBars - 1 + rangeLookback, atrLookback + 1).
if (atrLen != (int)atrLookback) {
    atrSum = 0.0;
    for (int i = 0; i < (int)atrLookback; ++i) {
        double hi = high[i] > close[i + 1] ? high[i] : close[i + 1];
        double lo = low[i] < close[i + 1] ? low[i] : close[i + 1];
        atrSum += hi - lo;
    }
    atrLen = (int)atrLookback;
} else {
    const int out = (int)atrLookback;
    double hiIn = high[0] > close[1] ? high[0] : close[1];
    double loIn = low[0] < close[1] ? low[0] : close[1];
    double hiOut = high[out] > close[out + 1] ? high[out] : close[out + 1];
    double loOut = low[out] < close[out + 1] ? low[out] : close[out + 1];
    atrSum += hiIn - loIn;
    atrSum -= hiOut - loOut;
}
atrVal = atrSum / (int)atrLookback;
okLong = true;
okShort = true;
for (ii = 0; ii <= (int)confirmBars - 1; ++ii) {
    lowestLow = low[ii + 1];
    highestHigh = high[ii + 1];
    for (kk = ii + 2; kk <= ii + (int)rangeLookback; ++kk) {
        if (el_lt(low[kk], lowestLow)) lowestLow = low[kk];
        if (el_gt(high[kk], highestHigh)) highestHigh = high[kk];
    }
    if (el_gt(close[ii], lowestLow - stopBuffer - bufferAtrMultiple * atrVal)) okLong = false;
    if (el_lt(close[ii], highestHigh + stopBuffer + bufferAtrMultiple * atrVal)) okShort = false;
}
